# Docker build context excludes (CFG-06).
#
# Both image builds (apps/api/Dockerfile, apps/web/Dockerfile) use the repo
# ROOT as their context (compose `context: ../..`, CI `context: .`). Without
# this file a developer- or operator-built image COPYs the whole workspace —
# embedding stale local node_modules/.next/dist, bloating the image and
# busting the build cache — and could ship a stray apps/*/.env. The Dockerfiles
# install deps and generate Prisma clients themselves, so none of this belongs
# in the context.

# Dependencies + build output (regenerated inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.prisma

# Secrets / local env — must never enter an image layer
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.prod.example

# Local dev + VCS noise
.git
.gitignore
.dev-storage
**/*.log

# Editor / OS cruft
**/.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Never let local Cloudflare-era files into an image.
**/.dev.vars
**/.wrangler
